.TH APER-SEARCH 1 "July 28, 2026" "aper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aper-search \- search bounded geometric substitution spaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-space " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-cells " count" ]
.RB [ \-\-candidate " index" ]
.RB [ \-\-bank " directory" ]
.RB [ \-c " scheme" ]
.RB [ \-n " depth" ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.br
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-space " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-cells " count" ]
.RB [ \-\-candidate " index" ]
.RB [ \-\-bank " directory" ]
.BR " " { \-\-definition | \-\-classify }
.br
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-space " name" ]
.RB [ \-\-cells " count" ]
.RB [ \-\-bank " directory" ]
.B \--list-candidates
.br
.B aper-search
.RB [ \-\-bank " directory" ]
.BR " " { \-l | \-\-list-known }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.BR aper-search " " { \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aper-search
enumerates a finite rule space, applies algebraic and geometric tests, checks
several generations, removes canonically equivalent rules, and writes one
survivor as a native vector PDF or declarative
.B .aper
system.
.PP
The default polyomino search enumerates every free connected polyomino of the
selected size.  For each shape P it places all integer-lattice rotations and
reflections inside the twofold inflation 2P, then uses exact cover to find
dissections of 2P into four copies of P.  Cell counts 1 through 6 are supported.
.PP
With three cells, the L-triomino result exactly rediscovers the separately
encoded Chair rule; the straight triomino is a periodic control.  The legacy
square and binary-square spaces remain explicit pipeline controls.  A survivor
or failed bank match is not evidence of novelty, nonperiodicity, or
aperiodicity.
.PP
The known-rule bank contains systems locally encoded as executable geometry.
In the source tree, the default
.I ./rules
directory contributes nine declarative rules and six legacy built-in fallbacks
complete a fifteen-system bank.  When no local rule directory is present, an
installed copy reads the same nine rules from
.IR PREFIX/share/aper/rules .
Classification tests exact canonical rule equivalence only; it does not detect
names, decorated refinements, mutual local derivability, or proofs of
aperiodicity.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \--space " " name
Search
.BR polyomino ,
.BR square ,
or
.BR binary-square .
The default is
.BR polyomino .
.TP
.BR \--cells " " count
Use polyominoes with 1 through 6 cells.
The default is 3.
This option is available only in the polyomino space.
.TP
.BR \--candidate " " index
Select a zero-based canonical survivor to render, serialise, or classify.
The default is 0.
.TP
.BR \--bank " " directory
Recursively load every
.B .aper
definition below
.I directory
into the known-rule bank, then add built-in systems as fallbacks.
Without this option, aper-search first tries
.I ./rules
and, when that directory is absent, the installed
.I PREFIX/share/aper/rules
bank.
.TP
.B \--list-candidates
Write deterministic tab-separated search statistics and every survivor with
its exact executable-bank match, if any.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-colour " " scheme
Select
.BR flare ,
.BR grove ,
.BR electric ,
or
.BR tide .
The default is
.BR flare .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-depth " " depth
Render the patch after 1 through 7 substitutions.
The default is 4.
This option is PDF-patch output only.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule
Render the discovered substitution rule instead of a finite patch.
.TP
.B \--definition
Write the selected candidate as a reusable declarative
.B .aper
system instead of PDF.
This serialises the search survivor, not a matching legacy bank entry.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-classify
Write a text classification of the selected survivor against the encoded
known-rule bank instead of rendering PDF.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list-known
List the local system identifier, Encyclopedia record, and source URL for every
source-linked rule in the composed executable bank.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect the complete three-cell search and render its Chair survivor:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --list-candidates
aper-search --candidate 0 > chair.pdf
aper-search --candidate 0 --rule > chair-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Make the discovered rule durable, then render it through the generic reader:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --candidate 0 --definition > chair.aper
aper --file chair.aper -n 5 > chair-from-file.pdf
.EE
.PP
Search dominoes and classify their survivors:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --cells 2 --list-candidates
aper-search --cells 2 --candidate 2 --classify
.EE
.PP
Run the labelled square control that contains the Thue-Morse rediscovery:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --space binary-square --list-candidates
aper-search --space binary-square --candidate 22 --classify
.EE
.PP
Classify against an explicitly selected declarative bank:
.PP
.EX
aper-search --bank rules --list-known
aper-search --bank rules --cells 5 --list-candidates
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./rules
First default recursively searched rule-bank directory when it exists.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/rules
Installed fallback rule-bank directory.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/encyclopedia.tsv
Metadata-only reference index of the Tilings Encyclopedia substitution pages;
it is not used for executable rule classification.
Installed separately by
.BR "make install-encyclopedia" .
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/encyclopedia.NOTICE.md
Attribution, licence, and transformation notice for the reference index.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aper-search
exits zero after writing the requested PDF, definition, classification, or
listing.  It exits non-zero if an argument or candidate index is invalid, a
search bound is exceeded, an invariant fails, or output cannot be written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aper (1)
